Subject: [PATCH 08526/11362] Fix dead SUBMITTED_EARLY_STOP_GRACE flag
 (2026-08-08 review, Gaps #1)

SUBMITTED_EARLY_STOP_GRACE=400 was set 2026-08-07 alongside the MAX_ACTIONS
raise, commented "Enabled," but was never read anywhere. E3AgentPolicy
neither accepted nor forwarded it to StepwiseExplorer, so every scored game
ran its fruitless post-solve tail to the full 2000-action budget while the
record claimed the wall-clock safeguard was on. Found independently by four
lenses of the 2026-08-08 adversarial review
(docs/research-notes/live-agent-adversarial-review-2026-08-08.md).

Threads early_stop_grace through E3AgentPolicy.__init__ into the
StepwiseExplorer construction, adds it to SUBMITTED_AGENT_CONFIG (and wires
that into the real scored construction site in make_carnot_agent), corrects
the misleading comment, and replaces analyze_arc_early_stop_sweep.py's
stale _flag_is_dead() (asserted the opposite of reality) with
_flag_wiring_state(), which inspects the live signature/config instead of
a hardcoded premise.

5 new tests in test_arc_early_stop_grace_wiring_20260808.py, including one
that spies on the StepwiseExplorer constructor call itself (not just the
resulting attribute) and one that spies on E3AgentPolicy inside the real
make_carnot_agent scored entrypoint. Adversarially verified independently
(separate agent, own test harness) as CONFIRMED_FIXED; re-verified myself
-- 5/5 pass, --no-cov, targeted files only.

Adds REQ-ARC-WMTE-6220 to the openspec capability. 12 results/*.json
artifacts get a freshness_acknowledgements entry: the fix only activates a
NEW code path for FUTURE runs (E3AgentPolicy forwarding the constant to
StepwiseExplorer's constructor); every historical artifact recorded agent
behavior from before this fix existed, when early-stopping was
structurally unreachable regardless of the constant's value. Verified via
scripts/arc_scored_path_early_stop_sweep.py, which already documents this
exact bug and works around it by setting early_stop_grace directly on the
constructed explorer -- never through the constructor path this fix adds
-- so the one artifact in this set that specifically studies this flag
(outer_loop_arc_early_stop_grace_sweep_20260726.json) is confirmed
unaffected by direct evidence, not just argument. One second-order cascade
(an artifact citing two of the acknowledged artifacts by hash) resolved the
same way.

