 {
- "experiment": "outer_loop_arc_gateway_accurate_rescore_20260726",
- "title": "GATEWAY-ACCURATE re-score: the opening RESET is FREE, so the published uncharged-RESET optimism was itself overstated",
- "run_date": "2026-07-30T11:03:57Z",
- "schema": "carnot.arc_gateway_accurate_rescore.v1",
- "charge_model_settled_from_installed_source": {
-  "source_spans": {
-   "gateway_charges_a_reset": "arc_agi/scorecard.py:701-704 `inc_reset_count` -> `self.resets[i] += 1` AND `self.actions[i] += 1`",
-   "but_only_when_full_reset_is_FALSE": "arc_agi/scorecard.py:834-843 `update_scorecard` -- a RESET frame routes to `new_play()` when `full_reset` else to `reset()`; only `reset()` reaches `inc_reset_count`",
-   "new_play_charges_nothing": "arc_agi/scorecard.py:692-699 `inc_play_count` APPENDS actions=0/resets=0 for a new play; it never increments an existing counter",
-   "full_reset_predicate_is_action_count_0_or_state_WIN": "arcengine/base_game.py:305-316 `handle_reset` sets `_full_reset` when `_action_count == 0` or `state == WIN`; `arc_agi/wrapper.py:187-195` gates the scorecard update on a non-empty frame and passes `resp.full_reset` through to `update_scorecard`",
